2:T541,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the best layout for a very small bathroom?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The best layout depends on the room shape, door, window and existing plumbing. Common solutions include a corner basin, short-projection toilet, compact shower and wall-mounted storage."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is a shower better than a bath in a small bathroom?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A shower usually uses less floor space, but a shower-bath can be a practical compromise if your household needs bathing facilities. The choice depends on the room dimensions and how the bathroom is used."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How can I add storage to a small bathroom?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Use vertical and recessed space with a mirrored cabinet, tall cupboard, vanity drawers, shower niche and wall hooks. Plan storage for towels and cleaning products before choosing the fittings."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can a professional make a small bathroom feel bigger?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Careful positioning of fittings, clear shower screens, continuous finishes, suitable lighting and well-planned storage can improve both the practical use and visual spaciousness of the room."}}]}7:["slug","bathroom-fitting-ideas-for-small-bathrooms","d"]
