e to practical fixtures, lighting and professional renovation tips.\",\"datePublished\":\"2026-07-30T07:04:10.971Z\",\"dateModified\":\"2026-07-30T07:04:10.971Z\",\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"BMB Renovation\",\"url\":\"https://bmbrenovation.co.uk\"},\"publisher\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"BMB Renovation\",\"url\":\"https://bmbrenovation.co.uk\",\"logo\":{\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\"url\":\"https://bmbrenovation.co.uk/og-image.png\"}},\"mainEntityOfPage\":\"https://bmbrenovation.co.uk/blog/bathroom-fitting-ideas-for-small-bathrooms\",\"keywords\":\"small bathroom ideas UK, small bathroom layout ideas, space-saving bathroom fittings, small bathroom storage ideas, compact bathroom renovation\"}"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://bmbrenovation.co.uk\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Blog\",\"item\":\"https://bmbrenovation.co.uk/blog\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"Bathroom Fitting Ideas for Small Bathrooms\",\"item\":\"https://bmbrenovation.co.uk/blog/bathroom-fitting-ideas-for-small-bathrooms\"}]}"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$2"}}],["$","$L3",null,{}],["$","section",null,{"className":"relative pt-28 pb-12 bg-gradient-to-br from-gray-900 via-gray-800 to-gray-900","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6","children":[["$","nav",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-white/50 mb-6","aria-label":"Breadcrumb","children":[["$","$L4",null,{"href":"/","className":"hover:text-[#C8A97E] transition-colors inline-flex items-center gap-1","children":[["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":24,"height":24,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-house w-3.5 h-3.5","children":[["$","path","5wwlr5",{"d":"M15 21v-8a1 1 0 0 0-1-1h-4a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v8"}],["$","path","1d0kgt",{"d":"M3 10a2 2 0 0 1 .709-1.528l7-5.999a2 2 0 0 1 2.582 0l7 5.999A2 2 0 0 1 21 10v9a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2z"}],"$undefined"]}]," Home"]}],["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":24,"height":24,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-chevron-right w-3 h-3","children":[["$","path","mthhwq",{"d":"m9 18 6-6-6-6"}],"$undefined"]}],["$","$L4",null,{"href":"/blog","className":"hover:text-[#C8A97E] transition-colors","children":"Blog"}],["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":24,"height":24,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-chevron-right w-3 h-3","children":[["$","path","mthhwq",{"d":"m9 18 6-6-6-6"}],"$undefined"]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-white/80 truncate max-w-[200px] sm:max-w-none","children":"Bathroom Fitting Ideas for Small Bathrooms"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-white/10 border border-white/10 text-[#C8A97E] text-xs mb-4","children":"bathroom fitting ideas for small bathrooms"}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"font-display text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight leading-tight","children":"Bathroom Fitting Ideas for Small Bathrooms"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2 text-white/50 text-sm mt-5","children":[["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":24,"height":24,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-calendar w-4 h-4","children":[["$","path","1cmpym",{"d":"M8 2v4"}],["$","path","4m81vk",{"d":"M16 2v4"}],["$","rect","1hopcy",{"width":"18","height":"18","x":"3","y":"4","rx":"2"}],["$","path","8toen8",{"d":"M3 10h18"}],"$undefined"]}],"30 July 2026",["$","span",null,{"className":"text-white/25","children":"·"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"BMB Renovation"}]]}]]}]}],["$","article",null,{"className":"py-14 sm:py-20 flex-grow bg-gray-50","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-gray-100 p-6 sm:p-10","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["A small bathroom does not have to feel cramped or difficult to use. The right layout, carefully chosen fittings and well-planned storage can make a compact room feel calmer, brighter and more practical. Whether you are updating a cloakroom, refurbishing an en-suite or redesigning a family bathroom, the best results usually come from considering how every centimetre will be used before choosing tiles or taps. These bathroom fitting ideas for small bathrooms are suitable for many UK homes, including properties where awkward corners, narrow rooms and limited natural light create additional challenges."]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 tracking-tight mt-12 mb-4","children":"Start with the layout, not the fittings"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["Before selecting a basin or shower, measure the room carefully and mark the position of the door, window, soil pipe, radiator and existing water connections. Think about the clear space needed to open the door, sit comfortably on the toilet and step into the shower. A layout that looks good on paper may feel restrictive if several doors or drawers open into the same area. In some rooms, reversing the door swing or using a sliding or folding door can release valuable floor space, although the best option depends on the property and existing structure. Keeping the toilet and basin near their current plumbing positions may also help control the scope of the work, while moving fixtures can create a much better arrangement where the existing layout is particularly inefficient."]}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 tracking-tight mt-8 mb-3","children":"Layouts that often work well in compact bathrooms"}],["$","aside",null,{"className":"my-10 rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-br from-gray-900 via-gray-800 to-gray-900 p-6 sm:p-8 border border-[#C8A97E]/30","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight mb-2","children":"Thinking about your own project?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-white/70 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed mb-5","children":["BMB Renovation covers Watford, Bushey, Rickmansworth, St Albans, Hemel Hempstead and beyond — all trades in-house. Call +44 7775 758 717 or send us a message."]}],["$","$L4",null,{"href":"/contact","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] text-white text-sm font-bold hover:bg-[#b39668] transition-colors","children":["Get a Free Quote",["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":24,"height":24,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-arrow-right w-4 h-4","children":[["$","path","1ays0h",{"d":"M5 12h14"}],["$","path","xquz4c",{"d":"m12 5 7 7-7 7"}],"$undefined"]}]]}]]}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"my-5 space-y-2.5","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["A wall-hung or compact close-coupled toilet placed in a corner can leave a clearer route through the room."]}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["A corner basin can work well in a cloakroom, especially where a standard basin would interfere with the door."]}]]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["A walk-in shower or shower enclosure at the far end of a narrow room can make the space feel more open than a bath with a bulky screen."]}]]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["A shower-bath can provide bathing flexibility where the household needs a bath but the room cannot accommodate separate fixtures."]}]]}],["$","li","4",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["A sliding shower door or inward-folding enclosure can avoid the projecting door swing associated with some framed shower units."]}]]}],["$","li","5",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["A bath installed along the longest wall may be the most practical choice, with a wall-mounted toilet or basin helping to preserve visible floor area."]}]]}]]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 tracking-tight mt-12 mb-4","children":"Choose compact fittings without sacrificing comfort"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["Small fittings are useful, but the narrowest product is not automatically the best choice. A basin that is too shallow may cause splashing, while an undersized shower can be uncomfortable for everyday use. Look for proportions that suit the room and the people using it. Short-projection toilets, slim vanity units and compact baths can reduce obstruction without making the bathroom feel improvised. Wall-hung furniture and toilets can also create a more continuous floor line, making cleaning easier and helping the room appear less crowded. Concealed cisterns may provide a neat finish, but they need suitable access for maintenance, so the installation should be planned rather than boxed in without thought."]}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 tracking-tight mt-8 mb-3","children":"Use walls and corners for storage"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["In a small bathroom, storage should use vertical space wherever possible. A mirrored cabinet above the basin can combine everyday storage with the function of a mirror. Recessed shower niches can hold shampoo and soap without introducing a shelf that projects into the enclosure, provided the wall construction allows one to be formed properly. Tall, narrow cupboards can use an otherwise overlooked strip beside a basin or toilet. Open shelving is helpful for towels and attractive accessories, but too much visible storage can make a compact room look untidy. A vanity unit with drawers often gives easier access than a cupboard, while wall-mounted units keep more of the floor visible."]}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"my-5 space-y-2.5","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Plan a dedicated place for toilet rolls, cleaning products, towels and spare toiletries before finalising the furniture."]}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Use hooks on the back of the door or on an unused wall for towels and dressing gowns."]}]]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Consider a heated towel rail that suits the available wall width rather than allowing a large radiator to dominate the room."]}]]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Keep frequently used items within reach and store occasional-use products in taller or less accessible cupboards."]}]]}],["$","li","4",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Avoid filling every wall with shelves; a small room benefits from a controlled number of storage zones."]}]]}]]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 tracking-tight mt-12 mb-4","children":"Make a small bathroom feel larger"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["Light, continuity and visual simplicity can have a noticeable effect on how spacious a bathroom feels. Large-format tiles may reduce the number of grout lines, although they still need to be suitable for the wall dimensions and installed on an appropriately prepared surface. Pale wall colours, a consistent floor finish and clear glass shower panels can help maintain an uninterrupted view across the room. Gloss finishes reflect light, while matt surfaces can give a softer appearance and may be easier to live with depending on the product. A well-placed mirror can reflect light and increase the sense of depth, but it should be positioned for practical use rather than purely for visual effect. Good layered lighting is also important: ambient lighting, task lighting around the mirror and suitable illumination in the shower area should be designed with the room and installation requirements in mind."]}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 tracking-tight mt-8 mb-3","children":"Why professional planning matters"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["A compact bathroom leaves little room for errors. Uneven walls, concealed pipework, floor levels, ventilation and the position of electrical equipment can all affect which layout is achievable. A professional renovation company can assess the room, coordinate the fitting sequence and identify clashes before installation begins. This is especially useful when the project involves several trades, such as plumbing, tiling, electrical work and cabinet installation. BMB Renovation provides bathroom fitting and renovation in Watford and nearby areas, with all plumbing, tiling, electrical and cabinet installation work handled in-house. The company is based at 157 Judge Street, Watford WD24 5AN, and serves Watford, Bushey, Rickmansworth, St Albans, Hemel Hempstead, Borehamwood, Harrow, Croxley Green, Luton and Bedford. You can review the ",["$","$L4","0",{"href":"/bathroom-fitting-watford","className":"text-[#C8A97E] font-medium underline decoration-[#C8A97E]/40 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#C8A97E] transition-colors","children":"bathroom fitting service in Watford"}]," or see the wider range of ",["$","$L4","1",{"href":"/services","className":"text-[#C8A97E] font-medium underline decoration-[#C8A97E]/40 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#C8A97E] transition-colors","children":"renovation services"}]," before deciding what level of help your project needs."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["It is worth discussing practical details early, including whether the existing soil pipe can remain, where new pipework will run, how access panels will be provided and what type of ventilation the room requires. Your contractor should also explain which finishes are suitable for wet areas and how the work will be sequenced. A clear plan helps avoid choosing a basin that cannot be opened properly, a shower screen that blocks a towel rail or storage that prevents access to essential services. If you are comparing options in Hertfordshire, North London or Bedfordshire, BMB Renovation offers free, no-obligation quotes; you can ",["$","$L4","0",{"href":"/contact","className":"text-[#C8A97E] font-medium underline decoration-[#C8A97E]/40 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#C8A97E] transition-colors","children":"request a free quote"}]," once you have a rough idea of your preferred layout and fittings."]}],["$","aside",null,{"className":"my-10 rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-br from-gray-900 via-gray-800 to-gray-900 p-6 sm:p-8 border border-[#C8A97E]/30","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight mb-2","children":"Get a Free, No-Obligation Quote"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-white/70 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed mb-5","children":["BMB Renovation handles kitchens, bathrooms and full home renovations across Watford, Hertfordshire, North London & Bedfordshire — all trades in-house. Tell us about your project today."]}],["$","$L4",null,{"href":"/contact","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] text-white text-sm font-bold hover:bg-[#b39668] transition-colors","children":["Get My Free Quote",["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2